abstract: >-
  PIEC (Python Integrated Experimental Control) is an open-source,
  modular Python library for scalable laboratory automation.
  Built on a hierarchical, type-first architecture, PIEC
  standardizes hardware-agnostic instrument drivers and provides
  reusable measurement classes for coordinating laboratory
  instruments, acquiring data, and performing analysis.
  Its modular design supports rapid experimental prototyping,
  multi-instrument workflows, virtual instrumentation, and
  integration with AI/ML-driven systems for closed-loop and
  autonomous experimentation.
keywords:
